A||||5||Gold-86SE||2.5 Duke Head Question||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||06-22-2000||03:38 PM||||<BR>I have an '84 Duke, will a head from an '87 Duke fit and work on the '84 engine?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||06-22-2000||03:45 PM||||There were changes made in 87 to the duck in order to increase horse power from the duke. Now if this included head modifications i have no idea but im sure someone here does.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||06-22-2000||04:03 PM||||I don't know about any differences in the heads. To check, just take the valve cover off the '84 (if the head isn't already off of the motor) And see if the valve stems are the same length and rocker arms are the same as the '87.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||06-22-2000||05:23 PM||||The 87 head will definitely bolt to the 84 engine block.  I'm about 95% sure the 84 exhaust manifold will bolt to the 87 head as well.<P>However, I'm not sure if the bolt pattern on the intake side and/or intake ports were changed when Pontiac went to the aluminum intake manifold and hi-flow TBI unit in 1987.<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 06-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||06-23-2000||03:19 AM||||The intake manifolds are different. If the '87 had the 700 TBI then they are not  the same. Actually, I was told the heads were also different as I wanted to do this awhile back...but that is what I was told. I did not actually try it.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||06-23-2000||03:59 PM||||I'm not sure but I know that Race-Tech (The Fiero Shop)in Toronto would know. web page is  <A HREF="http://www.thefieroshop.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefieroshop.com</A>  or his phone number is 416-747-5728 ask for Joe.  He'll know.||||reg||1
